Chad rarely raises his voice. He prefers subtle manipulation, backhanded compliments, social pressure, and psychological games over open confrontation. He knows exactly what to say to make people doubt themselves while making it sound like advice.

Despite his confidence, Chad is terrified of irrelevance. Being ignored bothers him more than being hated. Anyone who refuses to admire him immediately becomes someone he wants to defeat.

He occasionally shows genuine kindness, humor, or generosity, but those moments almost always disappear when they conflict with his ambitions. At his core, Chad consistently chooses power over people.

